  "notes": [
    "Preregistered interpretation: monotone or consistently negative Standard10 movement with nonnegative CFR4 movement selects league/preservation-objective intervention; nonmonotone wide-noise curves select at most one deeper convergence control; broad positive curves reopen scale. The same fresh seed is reused across endpoints within a lineage to enable paired endpoint contrasts, while seeds 20261920-20261922 are untouched by prior evaluations.",
    "Added after experiment start and therefore separately artifact-hashed: raw-pair archive-curve auditor with SHA/count/key/deck/control identity gates, paired endpoint contrasts, seed-level t intervals, and prior-panel sign comparison."
  ],
  "result": {
    "summary": "Nine frozen archive evaluations completed over 73,728 hands. All 18,432 raw pair rows passed SHA, count, uniqueness, common-deck, and identical-control gates. The paired 149k-to-262k pooled change averaged -1.947 bb/100 across seeds with t95 CI [-17.051, 13.157]; Standard10 and CFR4 contrasts were also inconclusive.",
    "conclusion": "The preregistered selective Standard10 tradeoff hypothesis is rejected: neither key anchor has a coherent monotone curve, there is no statistically coherent broad decline or positive curve, and two of three lineages flip final common-anchor sign across independent fresh panels. Current approximately1k-pair-per-anchor frozen panels expose high between-deal and between-seed variance, not a mechanism-level reason to terminate a potentially long-horizon recipe.",
    "decision": "RUN_ONE_SEED_1M_DEEP_CONVERGENCE_CONTROL",
    "next_step": "Continue only Seed1, the sole lineage that passed the original 262k breadth and both-seat gate, from its exact 263,423-hand state to 1,048,576 actual hands. Preserve optimizer/replay/league/assignment state and use a nonoverlapping deal window; then require a larger frozen four-anchor both-seat panel before any replication or Slumbot spend."
  },
